  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "buyer/policy.py",
      "line": 389,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "[P1] Preserve the alternative guard in emergency closing. fallback_close() filters only must-haves, then accepts the cheapest sheet even when walking away is cheaper. runner calls this after any ArenaError from close(), so an API failure can turn a deliberate walk-away into a bad contract. Local reproduction: normal close walks on a EUR 334,628 offer versus a EUR 268,128 alternative, while fallback_close accepts that same offer. Reuse the same safe selection as normal closing, including supplier estimate and finite cost; refresh state after a conflict before choosing a currently valid offer. Add a regression test exercising the failed-close path, not just the helper."
