      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "[P1] Use the same cost inputs for eligibility and ranking. acceptable() is called without side.est, but the next line ranks with side.est. On stabilise/secure_supply this omits the relationship charge from the alternative check. In a modified S01 reproduction, the offer costs EUR 334,628 without the estimate and EUR 589,628 with it, versus a EUR 341,278 alternative; close() still accepts. Pass the estimate to the guard and ensure the cost used to select and log the deal is exactly the cost that passed the alternative check. Cover a relationship charge that reverses acceptance."
    },
    {
      "path": "buyer/runner.py",
      "line": 65,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "[P1] Budget writer time against all live thread deadlines. neg.move() synchronously calls the writer before sending; all other supplier clocks keep running. replied is initialized only after attachment downloads and setup, which also hides elapsed opening time. A 20-second writer per thread plus supplier latency can exhaust the later bidders' 60-second clocks, and keepalives currently cover only done threads. Track elapsed time from receipt, reserve send/close time, and skip the writer when the earliest live deadline has insufficient slack. Also enforce a wall-clock bound: httpx.Client(timeout=20) is an operation/inactivity timeout, not a total elapsed deadline, and paragraph() itself cannot interrupt a slow callable. Keep arena sends serialized; do not fix this by sending concurrent requests in one session. Test delayed setup, slow model/supplier calls, multiple bidders and no remaining message budget."
    },
    {
      "path": "buyer/runner.py",
      "line": 83,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "[P1] Handle a terminal result from a successful send before another move or close. The 409 path checks reply['result'], but the normal send path always appends the reply and continues. The kit's play() explicitly handles terminal results here (for example, the last supplier walking away). Otherwise we can call close() on an ended session, then call it again through the emergency path and lose an already available result. Save/return the terminal result immediately after committing the sent message. Add a fake-table regression asserting that close() is never called after send() returns a result."
    },
    {
      "path": "buyer/policy.py",
      "line": 87,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "[P2] Do not interpret the first component's should-cost as the bundle's unit cost. For a multi-part case, full_cost feeds near_cost, the relationship target and the supplier estimate, but this lookup uses only parts[0]. A component cost and a kit price are different units. Derive a bundle estimate only from documented composition/quantities or an explicit bundle-level cost. If those are absent, keep the estimate unknown and disable estimate-dependent decisions rather than inventing equal weights. Add tests for a known composition and a bundle whose composition is unavailable."
    }
  ]
}
EOF
